{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 8, "source_sha256": "97a5762517d882e71a4b27e5f74341ad631ceccef5de0af89187ba6c3d64ae64", "sanskrit": "vijñānahetavaḥ syurna tato'rthe dhīḥ prakalpyate yena || 7 ||", "translation": "They might be causes of cognition — but that by which a cognition of the object is not produced from it is not [such a cause].", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 9, "source_sha256": "6a0eb10fc645d004826e8d46925b6d7025c49a60f78422590f80a78a13f58236", "sanskrit": "yadvasturūpaprakhyāprabhāvitāḥ | vijñānahetavastatra tato'rthe dhīrna kalpyate ||  iti |", "translation": "Those [words] which are brought about by the appearance of the object's form — there, from them a cognition of the object is not constructed.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 10, "source_sha256": "568ad631d66069ce7a5caa37e0d19ab7f14792e6f3e4d39fe21a1c1cc9821a7f", "sanskrit": "tathāpyucyate | tato na vibhūrnityo vā kaścidarthapratipādako yuktaḥ, nitarāmeva sphoṭa iti || 7", "translation": "Nevertheless it is said: therefore no omnipresent or eternal conveyer of meaning whatsoever is admissible — still less the Sphoṭa — thus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 11, "source_sha256": "095dd25c670fbe8f1bb20f4e10e35ea7b875ec256c1b1a9f5a01d6265488a7f5", "sanskrit": "vācakamiṣṭamaduṣṭaṃ hetuścet sthūlaśabdajātasya || 8 ||", "translation": "If a denoter of the class of gross words is desired as an unimpaired cause…", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 12, "source_sha256": "4fcdc5c3b8d8f2e310b0067fca26dac0f825a7423f4a44db1b6400c720f32cdb", "sanskrit": "vijñānaṃ krameṇa vāsya gavāderarthasyāduṣṭamabhidhāyakamiṣyatāmiti || 8 ||", "translation": "Or let a cognition, in sequence, of an object such as 'cow' be accepted as an unimpaired denoter — thus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 13, "source_sha256": "0be18ea96116aa90762a78fa11f0d8731089c2e1358a0d6048e6184b30c8032b", "sanskrit": "tadvastu niravaśeṣamaviśeṣeṇaiva buddhyupārohi || 9 ||", "translation": "That object ascends into cognition, indeed, without remainder and without distinction.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 14, "source_sha256": "64e99cf2c43bceebe32a2c94a0f6e0ebc3a0d10a59fe732a907e1cb8e03dba3d", "sanskrit": "bāhyākāraviśeṣeṇa buddhyupārūḍhaṃ yataḥ || 9 ||", "translation": "Since it is taken up into cognition by the particularity of its external form.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 15, "source_sha256": "92c3e6b588f3b463c584f29ecad147cb155b221a2462cfaa026207fe9b603874", "sanskrit": "asya vimṛśyā vācyā bhedābhedairidaṃ ca sat kintu || 10 ||", "translation": "The denotandum of this is to be examined through differences and non-differences; and this is real — but…", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 16, "source_sha256": "47ff133852519ff405f6b5d64dd1463cd09776691d8361b9023f81340a3f8183", "sanskrit": "viśeṣaḥ | atrocyate- idaṃ ca sat kintviti || 10 ||", "translation": "The specific point. Here it is said: 'this is real, but —' thus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 17, "source_sha256": "2a26d7b7d81a97add9c1e926df0ec605306214e8d686f87c13b570fb8e5d6594", "sanskrit": "so'ntaḥsaṃjalpātmā nādaḥ siddho na viṣayabhāvena || 11 ||", "translation": "That nāda, whose essence is inner mental articulation, is established — not in the mode of being an object.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 18, "source_sha256": "99ae318a4527fb54d08862828fa43af8d620ca1d0f277665ffdf1fa4be3ca010", "sanskrit": "nādastasyā'pi vācyabuddhiṃ janayatīti vakṣyati kārikopasaṃhāre || 11 ||", "translation": "That nāda also produces the cognition of the denoted of that [word] — thus he will state at the conclusion of the kārikā.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 19, "source_sha256": "a54f562667f03eb852dad21d7db07fb5d5223fb98c78173bb91c5adc258cd5e0", "sanskrit": "dṛṣṭaṃ sadapyasat tad yasmādetena sadā parāmṛṣṭam || 12 ||", "translation": "That [object], though real and seen, is unreal — since it is always grasped by this [word].", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 20, "source_sha256": "65bb099a22165d96022906e19473d8ae4347b17f858aa08aec9f7d1f978e2205", "sanskrit": "sarvaṃ śabdena jāyate || (vā0 pa0 1|115) iti | kathaṃ punaḥ śrīmatparākhye -", "translation": "'Everything is born from the word' (Vākyapadīya 1.115), thus. How, then, [is it taught] in the glorious Parākhyā?", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 21, "source_sha256": "f4348bc8e206ef8d638e932884cd1744ea766f018344c86302f1690401449b16", "sanskrit": "nādābhivyañjakatvenopacārādityadoṣaḥ || 12 ||", "translation": "This is the fault: that [being] 'the manifester of nāda' [holds only] by secondary usage (upacāra).", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 22, "source_sha256": "0b2b09be53501ed956db29c38da58c3b99420afb03921d4ea701b538ac52d0ac", "sanskrit": "tatkāryaśarīrendriyavikṛteḥ pṛthagevamavyaktam || 13 ||", "translation": "Thus the unmanifest [nāda] is separate from its effect — the body, the senses, and [their] modification.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 23, "source_sha256": "77be8b42f3118033f87ba0768868896f2b78cbd2204a9b929431ae6603f1e6e3", "sanskrit": "guṇakāraṇatvenaiva siddheḥ, kāryāntarahetutve ca pramāṇābhāvāditi || 13 ||", "translation": "Because [nāda] is established precisely as the cause of the guṇas, and because there is no evidence for its being the cause of other effects — thus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 24, "source_sha256": "4bbe6c4689e19910aec94b3b76aa78bc2864a233ef3d6d7a8ad9972bda9b1962", "sanskrit": "vākyapade pravibhinnaḥ padārthabuddherasaṅkaro yasmāt || 14 ||", "translation": "Since in the sentence-word the cognitions of the word-meanings are well differentiated, [so that there is] no mixing.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 25, "source_sha256": "60c85fc5b916ad41e35cd989d4a53a2eab84fb46335a1f0562b4146c7073a1ee", "sanskrit": "vācakatvena sthūlaśabdavācya iti || 14 ||", "translation": "Thus, by virtue of its denotativeness, [nāda] is the denotandum of gross words.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 26, "source_sha256": "0832874a0b4dd5063e19a733ff5b56e58e1c2be29b2055af99605ced79da8cdd", "sanskrit": "bālairbhinnā nādā utpattyapavargayoginastena || 15 ||", "translation": "The ignorant distinguish the nādas [as separate]; [but] they are subject to arising and dissolution — therefore…", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 27, "source_sha256": "7b1e7f870183e535e0d58cfa5464f7b48120fb43026f21aa62267870f5088be0", "sanskrit": "sattvāste'pi nityaṃ, bruvanti te || iti | kimataḥ ? ityata āha- utpattyapavargeti | tena kāraṇena", "translation": "'Even those who [assert their] existence declare them eternal' — thus. What follows from this? To this he says: 'utpatti-apavarga' — by that reason…", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 28, "source_sha256": "fbbcb05df6929bfc8b67fffcf829cd579e927acb2256ea1ebb85f871ce41e2e7", "sanskrit": "utpattivināśadharmitvaṃ kāryatvameṣāṃ siddhamityarthaḥ || 15 ||", "translation": "The meaning is: their being effects — [i.e.,] their having the property of arising and destruction — is established.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 29, "source_sha256": "fd71870edcd7d1158e712d918588866e2c0b21ab56b7663775103744e3b56d4a", "sanskrit": "tatsiddho nādaḥ paraḥ sumaṅgalā mālinī mahāmāyā || 16 ||", "translation": "That supreme nāda is established — [it is] Sumaṅgalā, Mālinī, Mahāmāyā.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 30, "source_sha256": "1985faae1a3f4d8e8793da26b3858ac6c3e92c9b16b588d5a0475cfb0f340874", "sanskrit": "vidyākhyaṃ tattvamityuktaṃ taistaistadāgameṣvittham || 17 ||", "translation": "In those various scriptures concerning it, [the nāda] is thus called the principle named Vidyā.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 31, "source_sha256": "3766fa698b6ec7dd530aea61a3ee94052962a8606e698bb1fa7d46b112adfb5c", "sanskrit": "iha punaranyaivoktā puruṣāsamavāyinī vāg yasmāt || 18 ||", "translation": "Here, however, a different speech is taught — one not inherent in the person — since…", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 32, "source_sha256": "978ebe3d1c39817ccff222e4ee0ea57d141b8aa187a750d5b008881d9cf88aa9", "sanskrit": "yuktam, pariṇāmitvaprasaṅgāt; tasmānnaiveyamatroktā || 18 ||", "translation": "It is proper — because of the consequence of transformation; therefore this is indeed not taught here.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 33, "source_sha256": "b94a05a8b599d1849d8612f724b54692426815332d088826865db59a6785e204", "sanskrit": "bahudhā sthātuṃ yadvā caitanyavinākṛtau vikāritvāt || 19 ||", "translation": "[Speech] cannot stand in many ways — or [there would be] the destruction of consciousness — because of its being subject to modification.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 34, "source_sha256": "fec4191cfe0a3dd65da8eb87c980fb18ce9a2f49d4ceddac28c08a1205d33f66", "sanskrit": "tasmāt pratipuruṣāttacchakteśca bhinnākuṇḍalinī nādakāraṇaṃ siddheti || 19 ||", "translation": "Therefore the Kuṇḍalinī, distinct from each person and from his power, is established as the cause of nāda — thus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 35, "source_sha256": "bd3fc5a427e8fb261b25cb1f50670f57a65609a00dae966d66909953db861047", "sanskrit": "acidapi śuddhatvānmāyāto'pyanyā tadūrdhvagā kathitā || 20 ||", "translation": "Though unconscious, [she] is taught as other than even Māyā, because of [her] purity, and as going above it.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 36, "source_sha256": "dcc328eb14c87758784d4fcb14ad1b90716810b1720af874d1fcf5324ceaedad", "sanskrit": "yaduktam - māyopari mahāmāyā (rau0 saṃ0 4|28) iti || 20 ||", "translation": "As it was said: 'Mahāmāyā is above Māyā' (Rauravāgama, Saṃhitā 4.28) — thus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 37, "source_sha256": "c8cc6dfaec2e0746278dc01d6175a8f2fb28497d61298487d9ca7339e50fd3f6", "sanskrit": "adhvanyuktaṃ cānyaiḥ sadāgamaiḥ śreyase ca taddhetuḥ || 21 ||", "translation": "And it is stated in the adhvan by other true scriptures, and it is the cause of the supreme good.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 38, "source_sha256": "7e333623fbef4619fc4ce00666bcf7dc4a3b73cb6fc607cac5dee77de4fa094a", "sanskrit": "yadāhuḥ- śabdabrahmaṇi niṣṇātaḥ paraṃ brahmādhigacchati (mai0 u0 6|22 ) iti || 21", "translation": "As they say: 'One who is steeped in the Word-Brahman attains the supreme Brahman' (Maitrāyaṇīya Upaniṣad 6.22) — thus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 39, "source_sha256": "684600217ec95840b6f6c58de075d3b62afa27e38aedbebd573c80a7d7e07d06", "sanskrit": "siddhirmuktiśca parā nādajñānakriyā ca saphaleti || 22 ||", "translation": "Perfection, liberation, and the supreme knowledge-and-action of nāda — and these are fruitful — thus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 40, "source_sha256": "52989d26a05dd3cc5e79f4db9514893587f060a8794e1156b27d854a34facc77", "sanskrit": "kathayantīti pūrvakriyānuṣaṅgaḥ || 22 ||", "translation": "'They declare' — thus [is] the carry-over of the earlier verb.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 41, "source_sha256": "6f68b82302a000464744b289eabf66f219106fa37b20273c0528b97279b51e23", "sanskrit": "tatkāryamabhiṣvaṅgād dṛkkriyayormīlanācca bhinnaṃ yat || 23 ||", "translation": "Its effect, which is different from attachment and from the union of seeing and acting…", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 42, "source_sha256": "7fc8994ca15716f5f4072b72d245fb694998e026e748f66c27fae8f56c477829", "sanskrit": "tattvaparikalpanābhāvaprasaṅgācca || 23 ||", "translation": "and because there would follow the non-postulation of any principle (tattva).", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 43, "source_sha256": "a2da69c4c3bd89320f12c86e55cc4d48e19d930b49290b8a5b82c1369a39db4b", "sanskrit": "yena sthūlaṃ śabdaṃ mantraṃ tantrātmakaṃ pravartate vāpi || 24 ||", "translation": "By which the gross word, the mantra, and the tantra-natured [sound] are set in motion — or also…", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 44, "source_sha256": "49e421ffafbd5789028abcbe46eddb47ef9a20944a9450f7d30e18b46ab25714", "sanskrit": "sthūlasya tu tadabhivyañjakatvād vācakatvamityuktam || 24 ||", "translation": "But for the gross word, denotativeness is said [to hold] because it manifests that [nāda].", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 45, "source_sha256": "350cd0b2955ebc7b2192c6ff36031e35408316210422709e0909ed3626c1e690", "sanskrit": "vācakajātaṃ nirmāyāntaratastad vyanakti bāhye'pi || 25 ||", "translation": "Having created the class of denoters, it manifests that within — and also externally.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 46, "source_sha256": "0cc8d11a6a939e57a34ebd263427a1cca3123733e41286d1fc72ae9ac8dd14e5", "sanskrit": "vācyavibhinnāṃ buddhiṃ kurvanto vardhayanti janayātrām || 26 ||", "translation": "Producing a cognition differentiated by the denotandum, they increase the course of birth-and-death.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 47, "source_sha256": "02f5dacbd9ca0d1265ae6a85ee6097da2ac1c6d1e47b7e5e4857f7fc02eac41e", "sanskrit": "nārāyaṇakaṇṭhasutaḥ kāśmīre vṛttapañcaviṃśatyā || 27 ||", "translation": "[Rāmakaṇṭha,] the son of Nārāyaṇakaṇṭha, in Kashmir, with the Vṛttapañcaviṃśati…", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
{"work": "nadakarika", "verse_idx": 48, "source_sha256": "18d7f4346fabb2c57e68b5e233379b92c1505f8438ad3502b8999741b0a9fbcd", "sanskrit": "vyākhyātā nādasiddhiśca prārthitena guruttamaiḥ ||", "translation": "And the Nādasiddhi was explained [by him] at the request of the foremost gurus.", "status": "MACHINE_PROPOSED", "ts": "2026-08-13T15:38:46"}
